# WASM build artifacts (regenerated by wasm-pack)
crates/wasm/pkg/
docs/chat/pkg/
# On-demand source documents staged by crates/wasm/build.rs (copies of the
# registered USC title USLM XML; served at /sources/<file>)
crates/wasm/sources/
# .prx.gz distribution artifacts emitted by the `emit_prx` example (#256).
# Build outputs published to the GitHub release + Pages /ontologies/, never
# committed (rkyv wire layout is toolchain-dependent; the canonical source
# of truth stays the bundled .owl + its praxis.lock pin).
dist/
# E2E click-to-load staging: same `.prx.gz` artifacts, emitted into the
# pr4xis-web tree so the local/CI dual-load test has them at /ontologies/.
crates/wasm/ontologies/
# Parse-once corpus cache: `.prx.gz` archives emitted by `pr4xis compile`
# and read by the corpus loader instead of re-parsing source XML per
# process. Build output, never committed; CI restores it from the
# praxis.lock-keyed data cache.
#
# Written as `/*` rather than `/`, because git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY — a `!` re-include beneath one is silently inert.
.prx-cache/*
# …EXCEPT the statutory-definition overlays, which ARE committed.
#
# These nine files (56 KB total) are the output of `pr4xis compile --defines`,
# a derivation praxis.lock's own note measures at roughly 3.3 hours — far too
# long to be a build step, and nothing in CI ran it. The rest of `.prx-cache`
# is a speed optimisation whose absence costs time; this part is not. When it
# is missing, `USC_DEFINES_OVERLAY` is emitted EMPTY and the shipped wasm
# silently cannot answer a statutory definition — 5,443 definitions, 2,241 of
# them in Title 42, present on every developer's machine and absent from the
# artifact anyone else actually runs.
#
# Committing them is safe because they are content-addressed: every byte is
# pinned in praxis.lock's [compact_defines_signatures] and the loader refuses
# fail-closed on any mismatch. Regenerate with `pr4xis compile --defines --lock`.
!.prx-cache/usc-defines-compact/
.prx-cache/usc-defines-compact/*
!.prx-cache/usc-defines-compact/*.defines.cprx.gz

# Managed external data — fetched via `pr4xis update`, never committed
crates/domains/data/wordnet/*.xml
crates/domains/data/wordnet/*.xml.gz
# AGID inflection database (Atkinson 2016) — the 3.3 MB source is fetched; only
