crates/domains/data/legal/uscode/**/*.xml
crates/domains/data/legal/uscode/**/*.xml.gz
crates/domains/data/legal/uscode/**/*.zip
# W3C XML Schema Test Suite — 4.2 MB tar.gz, ~14k schema files,
# fetched via `pr4xis update`. SHA-256 pinned in praxis.lock.
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xsts/*.tar.gz
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xsts/xmlschema2006-11-06/
# W3C XML 1.0 Conformance Test Suite (XMLConf) — 624 KB tar.gz,
# ~3,000 XML test files. SHA-256 pinned in praxis.lock.
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xmlconf/*.tar.gz
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xmlconf/xmlconf/

# Claude Code transient files
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# cargo-mutants output — per-run, regenerated by dev-mutants
mutants.out/
# CatVar derivational-variation database (Habash & Dorr 2003) — the 1.1 MB source
# is fetched; only the LICENSE + README provenance records are committed.
crates/domains/data/morphology/catvar21.signed
# OWL ontology vocabularies (SPAR CiTO/DoCO/C4O/BiRO, W3C PROV-O, OLiA) — the
# raw RDF/XML `.owl` is FETCHED via `pr4xis update` (pinned in praxis.lock) and
# never committed; only the compiled, content-addressed compact `.prx.gz` ships
# (committed alongside, the runtime fast-load artifact every OWL-vocab consumer
# loads through the fail-closed `[compact_archive_signatures]` gate).
crates/domains/data/ontologies/*.owl

# Phase 2 raw schema / data sources (XSD / DTD / Adobe Glyph List) — the raw
# bytes are FETCHED via `pr4xis update` (pinned in praxis.lock `[hashes]`) and
# never committed; only the content-addressed committed `.prx` ships alongside,
# loaded through the generalized fail-closed `[compact_archive_signatures]` gate
# (`applied::data_provisioning::raw_source_prx`). Each source's runtime loader
# embeds the committed `.prx` via `include_bytes!`, never the raw.
crates/domains/data/legal/uscode/schema/uslm-1.0.18.xsd
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/mods/mods_3_8-2018.xsd
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xhtml/xhtml-1.0-strict.xsd
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/lmf/wn_lmf_dtd-1.3.dtd
crates/domains/data/adobe/glyphlist.txt
# Phase 2c — W3C XML schema / spec sources read at COMPILE time by build.rs
# (which now decodes their committed `.prx` through the same content gate) and
# at runtime via the embedded committed `.prx`. FETCHED from www.w3.org, pinned
# in praxis.lock `[hashes]`; only the content-addressed `.prx` ships.
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xml/xml.xsd
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xml/xml-infoset.xhtml
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xml/xml_1_0_fifth_edition-2008.xml
# Phase 2d FETCHED raw schema source — W3C XSD meta-schema. Routed through the
# generalized raw-source `.prx` path; the raw is fetch-only (pinned in
# praxis.lock `[hashes]`), only the `.prx` ships.
crates/domains/data/markup-schemas/xsd/xsd_meta_schema-1.1.xsd
# NOTE: the ECMA-376 OOXML schema ZIP is NOT gitignored — it is a BUNDLED
# source-of-truth (a ZIP-of-ZIPs the single-`.xml`-member `unzip_single_xml`
# fetch path cannot reproduce), so it is git-tracked like ewmh-wm-state.tsv /
# math-operators.xml: present on checkout so `fetch_entry` verifies the local
# copy and never downloads, excluded from the published crate by the
# `[package].include` allowlist, shipped only as the committed `.prx`.
# Phase 3 color-scheme COLLECTION — the Tinted Theming `tinted-schemes` corpus
# (formerly a git submodule, sourced from the i-am-logger/tinted-schemes fork).
# `pr4xis update` clones the theme tree into `data/tinted-schemes/` (TRANSIENT,
# ignored) and `theme_collection::archive_directory` flattens it into the
# deterministic `tinted-schemes-2025.themes` archive. Unlike a single-file HTTP
# download, a git-clone-and-archive is NOT byte-reproducible against the pin (the
# fork moves; archive ordering), so the `.themes` is a BUNDLED source-of-truth:
# git-tracked (the curated snapshot the `[hashes]` pin + `.prx` derive from),
# excluded from the published crate by the `[package].include` allowlist, present
# on a fresh checkout so `pr4xis update` verifies it locally instead of re-cloning
# the fork. Only the content-addressed `.prx` (data/themes/*.prx) ships.
crates/domains/data/tinted-schemes/

# VerbNet class-hierarchy COLLECTION (Kipper, Korhonen, Ryant & Palmer 2008),
# tag `vn-3.3` of github.com/cu-clear/verbnet. `pr4xis update` clones the
# tagged checkout into `data/verbnet-checkout/` (TRANSIENT, ignored) and
# `verbnet_class_collection::archive_directory` flattens its `verbnet3.3/`
# class-XML directory into the deterministic `verbnet-3.3.verbnet` archive.
# Same reasoning as tinted-schemes above: a git-clone-and-archive is NOT
# guaranteed byte-reproducible against the pin (GitHub's tarball packaging
# can drift even for a fixed tag), so the `.verbnet` is a BUNDLED
# source-of-truth: git-tracked, excluded from the published crate, present on
# a fresh checkout so `pr4xis update` verifies it locally instead of
# re-cloning. Only the content-addressed `.prx` (data/verbnet/*.prx) ships.
crates/domains/data/verbnet-checkout/

# ConceptNet 5.7.0 assertions (Speer, Chin & Havasi 2017), fetched from the
# versioned S3 object at s3.amazonaws.com/conceptnet/downloads/2019/edges/
# conceptnet-assertions-5.7.0.csv.gz (~475 MiB, 34M rows, no official
# English-only or WordNet-linked subset exists). The full raw download is
# TRANSIENT staging, never committed: `data/conceptnet-download/` holds the
# fetched .csv.gz, and the WordNet-crosswalk filter (mirrors VerbNet's
# `_wordnet_crosswalk.tsv` approach) produces the small, deterministic,
# committed subset — only assertions where both endpoints resolve to a loaded
# English/WordNet lemma survive. Only the filtered, content-addressed
# `.prx` (data/conceptnet/*.prx) ships.
crates/domains/data/conceptnet-download/

# FrameNet 1.7 (Baker, Fillmore & Lowe 1998), fetched from the NLTK-mirrored,
# checksum-verified release at raw.githubusercontent.com/nltk/nltk_data/
# gh-pages/packages/corpora/framenet_v17.zip (~99 MiB compressed / ~855 MiB
# uncompressed, dominated by an annotated-sentence corpus no part of this
# extraction needs). The full raw download is TRANSIENT staging, never
# committed: `data/framenet-download/` holds the fetched .zip, and the
# extraction (each LU file's root `<lexUnit>` start-tag attributes + every
# `frRelation.xml` relation row) produces the small, deterministic, committed
# subset. Only the extracted, content-addressed `.prx` (data/framenet/*.prx)
# ships.
crates/domains/data/framenet-download/

# SUMO WordNet↔SUMO mappings (Niles & Pease 2001, 2003), fetched from
# ontologyportal/sumo master at raw.githubusercontent.com/ontologyportal/sumo/
# master/WordNetMappings/WordNetMappings30-{noun,verb,adj,adv}.txt (~22 MiB
# across the four annotated-WNDB files). The full raw download is TRANSIENT
# staging, never committed: `data/sumo-download/` holds the fetched .txt files,
# and the extraction (synset offset + POS + each `&%<term><suffix>` annotation)
# produces the small, deterministic, committed subset. Only the extracted,
# content-addressed `.prx` (data/sumo/*.prx) ships.
crates/domains/data/sumo-download/

# PropBank predicate argument-structure frames (Palmer, Gildea & Kingsbury
# 2005; Bonial, Bonn, Conger, Hwang & Palmer 2014), tag `v3.4.0` of
# github.com/propbank/propbank-frames. `pr4xis update` clones the tagged
# checkout into `data/propbank-checkout/` (TRANSIENT, ignored) and
# `propbank_frameset_collection::archive_directory` flattens its `frames/`
# directory (7,565 real frame `.xml` files, excluding `.gitignore`/
# `README.txt`/`frameset.dtd`) into the deterministic `propbank-3.4.0.propbank`
# archive. Same reasoning as verbnet-checkout above: a git-clone-and-archive
# is NOT guaranteed byte-reproducible against the pin (GitHub's tarball
# packaging can drift even for a fixed tag), so the `.propbank` is a BUNDLED
# source-of-truth: git-tracked, excluded from the published crate, present on
# a fresh checkout so `pr4xis update` verifies it locally instead of
# re-cloning. Only the content-addressed `.prx` (data/propbank/*.prx) ships.
crates/domains/data/propbank-checkout/

